The plan is saved at `/outputs/clinic-test-2/sprint/sprint-plan.md`. Every P1/must story finishes in sprints 1–7, before DL-1 (2027-02-22).

**How I got there**
- The solver first said INFEASIBLE with DL-1 as a hard deadline. Its only verified option was OPT-1, "treat DL-1 as a soft target", so I applied it.
- I put all 28 Release 2 (P2/should) stories out of the horizon, because your request asks for them to go to sprint 8 or later.
- The solver returned OPTIMAL with no must-have after DL-1.
- A looser run with fewer Release 2 pins put the must-have S-POLISH-001 in sprint 8, so I discarded it.

**Sprints** (points are committed against P85 capacity; the sprint goal is one outcome users can see)

| Sprint | Committed / P85 | Goal |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | 35 / 28.4 | Staff can sign in with a username and password, and each role sees only what it needs. |
| 2 | 34 / 28.4 | A patient who signs in with a phone code and books gets an immediate SMS or WhatsApp confirmation. |
| 3 | 25 / 25.2 | A patient can see their upcoming appointments, cancel one, and open one from a message link. |
| 4 | 26 / 25.2 | A patient can reschedule into a free slot, and reminders follow the change. |
| 5 | 29 / 28.4 | A patient can find a free slot and book it on a phone, and the same slot is never booked twice. |
| 6 | 25 / 25.2 | Reception sees their clinic's day, and each dentist sees their own day. |
| 7 | 27 / 28.4 | Reception can mark patients arrived or no-show, and book, move and cancel for patients. |
| 8 | 0 / 28.4 | Empty. It could take the first Release 2 stories. |

Sprint 1 also carries the setup and foundation work for every module, and the sprint 7 and earlier polish stories are supporting work, not goals.

**Risks**
- Every sprint is at or above 95% of its P85 capacity. Sprints 1 and 2 are the most exposed, at 123% and 120%.
- The must-have work is 191 points against about 190 points of P85 capacity in sprints 1–7. If velocity drops to P85, sprint 7 slips first. That means reception booking, SMS delivery operations and the polish stories, and they would land after DL-1.
- Capacity is a cold-start estimate with low confidence.

**Deferred:** All 28 Release 2 stories (family members, repeat no-show block, WhatsApp-to-SMS fallback, no-show report). Each has a plain explanation in the plan. Nothing is deferred for a missing estimate or for being too large.

**Forecast:** The whole backlog finishes at P50 in sprint 10 (2027-04-04) and at P85 in sprint 11 (2027-04-18).

**Decisions for you**
- Whether to start Release 2 in sprint 8.
- Whether to cut about 10 points of must-have scope to give sprints 1–2 some slack.

